<title>USA: Buffalo, N.Y., loses appeal on teachers' pay.</title>
<headline>Buffalo, N.Y., loses appeal on teachers' pay.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Buffalo, N.Y., will have to pay its teachers federation back pay and raises as the state court of appeals declined to hear an appeal after the city lost a lawsuit.</p>
<p>Buffalo Teachers' Federation will get $200 million under the contract, but Mayor Anthony Masiello says the city does not have the money to pay them.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
